      "controversial_points": "The core conflict pits market‑driven deregulation against state‑led climate ambition. Conservatives demand cheap energy and nuclear revival, while the left insists on rapid renewable expansion and anti‑nuclear stance. Regional authorities clash with federal planners over grid investment priorities, exposing a north‑south divide on infrastructure funding. Industry groups pressure the government for cheaper electricity, while environmental NGOs warn that price cuts undermine climate targets. International supply concerns link gas and hydrogen strategies to geopolitical alignment, creating tension between security advocates and climate purists."
